            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Bengali for a chapter of a book, then the Bengali for a publisher."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: পৃষ্ঠা",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "পৃষ্ঠা — prishṭhā — \"a page\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "বইটার প্রথম পৃষ্ঠায় লেখকের ছবি আছে। bôiṭār prothom prishṭhāy lekhôker chhôbi āchhe. There is a picture of the writer on the first page of the book."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "পৃষ্ঠা (prishṭhā) is Sanskrit pṛṣṭha, 'the back; the upper side, a surface' (Monier-Williams); the sense 'a page', one face of a leaf, is the later one. Everyday speech also says পাতা."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
